diff -ruN a/debian/nmap.NEWS b/debian/nmap.NEWS
--- a/debian/nmap.NEWS
+++ b/debian/nmap.NEWS
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+nmap (7.992-1) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  freshdeb: changes since the distributions' versions (Ubuntu 22.04 has
+  7.80) that can affect scripts and automation:
+
+   * ncat in connect mode no longer half-closes the connection by default
+     when its input ends; -k (--keep-open) brings the old behaviour back
+     (7.96). In listen mode it no longer signals its process group (7.992).
+   * A host is no longer considered down because of an ICMP host
+     unreachable; other probes decide (7.92).
+   * nmap-update and the NSE script hostmap-bfk are gone (7.90, 7.991);
+     hostmap-crtsh reports only real subdomains unless hostmap-crtsh.lax
+     is set (7.98). Custom scripts using the IPP library's connect and
+     close functions need updating (7.98).
+   * Zenmap and Ndiff run on Python 3 (7.94).
+   * Since 7.90 nmap is licensed under the Nmap Public Source License
+     (/usr/share/doc/nmap-common/copyright).
+
+  Upstream's changelog has every change: https://nmap.org/changelog
+
+ -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
